    "foam": {
      "word": "FOAM",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The white substance, consisting of an aggregation of bubbles, which is formed on the surface of liquids,or in the mouth of an animal, by violent agitation or fermentation; froth; spume; scum; as, the foam of the sea. Foam cock, in steam boilers, a cock at the water level, to blow off impurities.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To gather foam; to froth; as, the billows foam. He foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth. Mark ix. 18.",
          "partOfSpeech": "intransitive verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To form foam, or become filled with foam; -- said of a steam boiler when the water is unduly agitated and frothy, as because of chemical action.",
          "partOfSpeech": "intransitive verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To cause to foam; as,to foam the goblet; also (with out), to throw out with rage or violence, as foam. \"Foaming out their own shame.\" Jude 13.",
          "partOfSpeech": "transitive verb"
        }
      ],
